  "$comment": "Star-data incident switch shared by apps/web (imported at build time via apps/web/lib/data-quality.ts), packages/api-server (read from disk via src/utils/data-quality.ts) and the public /v1 proxy. THREE measured GitHub-side changes degraded event-derived metrics. (1) 2025-05-24: a uniform ~32% volume cut across ALL event types with the event MIX PRESERVED - fewer events, same proportions. (2) 2025-10-09 (day-exact, atomic): payload trimming. PR additions/deletions/changed_files, push size/distinct_size, pr_merged and pr_merged_at arrive as 0 or the 1970 epoch sentinel. 0 means UNKNOWN here, not zero. ClickHouse daily: 2025-10-08 = 96.2% of PRs carried additions, 2025-10-09 = 0%. Fixing pagination does NOT restore these fields. (3) 2026-03..2026-07: progressive collapse of the event MIX. The /events feed is partitioned by POSITION - offsets 1-100 are a ~97% PushEvent block, the healthy mix only appears at offsets 101-300, hard-capped at 300 items total (per_page is clamped to 100). Our ETL read only offsets 1-100, so WatchEvent/month fell 2,223,459 (2026-02) -> 69,004 (2026-08). 'blocked' = rankings/leaderboards whose ORDER is now noise; served as HTTP 200 with an empty result and status:'unavailable' plus a pointer to a healthy alternative endpoint. 'tainted' = event-derived series that are LOWER BOUNDS; served normally with status:'degraded'. Flip active to false once the ETL reads offsets 1-300 and the affected windows are re-materialized, or once rankings move to stargazerCount snapshot deltas.",
